Privacy Policy for Image Compressor: MB to KB

Last updated: June 2, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how the App handles your information. By using the
App, you agree to this Privacy Policy.

1. SUMMARY
Image Compressor: MB to KB compresses and resizes your photos directly on your device. Your
photos are processed locally and are not uploaded to our servers or shared with us. The App
does not require an account, and we do not ask for your name, email, or contact details.

2. INFORMATION WE DO NOT COLLECT
- We do not collect, store, or transmit your photos. All compression, resizing, and format
  conversion happen on your device. Compressed copies are saved only on your device (your
  gallery and the App's local history).
- We do not require you to create an account or provide personal information.
- We do not access any photos other than the ones you choose within the App.

3. PERMISSIONS
The App may request the following so it can function:
- Photos and media: to let you select images to compress and to save compressed results to
  your device. On newer Android versions, the App uses the system photo picker, which grants
  access only to the specific images you select.
These permissions are used solely to provide the App's features.

4. INFORMATION COLLECTED BY THIRD PARTIES (ADS AND SERVICES)
The App may display advertisements and may use third-party services such as Google AdMob and
Google Play Services. When ads or these services are active, they may automatically collect
certain information, including:
- Device and usage information (e.g., device model, operating system, app version, language,
  and general usage events)
- A mobile advertising identifier (Advertising ID)
- IP address and coarse (non-precise) location derived from it
- Identifiers used to deliver and measure advertising
This information is collected and processed by those third parties under their own privacy
policies, mainly to display and measure ads and to keep their services secure. We do not
control the data practices of these third parties.
Google's Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy

5. HOW INFORMATION IS USED
- To provide the App's on-device compression and resizing features.
- To display and measure advertising through third-party ad networks (if enabled).
- To maintain, secure, and improve the App.

6. DATA SHARING AND SELLING
We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share your photos with anyone.
Information collected by third-party advertising or service providers is handled under their
own policies.

7. DATA RETENTION
Photos and compression history are stored only on your device and remain until you delete
them (you can clear history within the App or delete files from your device). We do not
retain your photos on any server.

8. SECURITY
Your photos are processed and stored on your device, so you remain in control of them. No
method of electronic storage is 100% secure, but the App is designed to keep image processing
local to your device.

9. CHILDREN'S PRIVACY
The App is not directed to children under the age of 13 (or the minimum age required in your
country). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a
child has provided personal information, please contact us and we will take appropriate steps.

10. YOUR CHOICES
- You can reset or delete your Advertising ID and opt out of personalized ads in your device
  settings (Settings -> Google -> Ads).
- You can clear the App's history and delete compressed files at any time.
- You can uninstall the App to stop all processing.

11. INTERNATIONAL USERS
The App may be used worldwide. Data collected by third-party services may be processed in
countries other than yours, as described in those providers' policies.

12. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Updates will be posted at this URL with a
revised "Last updated" date. Continued use of the App after changes means you accept the
updated policy.

